                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt has once again, without the slightest hesitation, claimed the top spot as the greatest game I've ever played. This game is simply perfect!\r\n\r\nThis is my fourth playthrough, and somehow, it still feels like I'm playing a game that was released yesterday. You know that feeling when you're incredibly hyped for a game you've been waiting years to play? That's exactly how The Witcher 3 still makes me feel, even after returning to the Continent time and time again.\r\n\r\nThe sheer number of quests scattered across the map and Witcher contracts available is incredible. The game makes you want to do absolutely everything all over again, even when you already know what awaits you. Exploration remains fantastic, easy to get into, and incredibly addictive. Whether you're hunting for hidden treasures, exploring caves, or discovering places you missed on previous playthroughs, there's always something that makes you want to keep exploring.\r\n\r\nAnother reason I keep coming back is Gwent. It's an incredibly fun card game with simple mechanics that are easy to learn, yet surprisingly engaging gameplay that can keep you entertained for hours. Sometimes, saving the world can wait a little, right?\r\n\r\nThe open world of The Witcher 3 was already gorgeous, but the next-gen update made it absolutely breathtaking. The vegetation, colors, shadows, and numerous other visual elements have all been significantly improved, making the experience even more impressive.\r\n\r\nToussaint, which was already a vibrant, colorful, and beautiful region, looks even more stunning. The way sunlight filters through the trees of Velen or reflects off the waters of Toussaint creates some truly spectacular scenery. The global illumination and lighting effects bring even more life to this world, turning exploration into a visual treat.\r\n\r\nIt's incredible how a game released so many years ago can still feel so modern, beautiful, and immersive. Very few games manage to deliver that feeling, especially after so many hours of adventure.\r\n\r\nNow all we can do is hope that this new story set in the region of Letten will be just as flawless and memorable as Hearts of Stone and Blood and Wine or, who knows, perhaps even better! If CD Projekt RED maintains this level of dedication and attention to detail, we're surely in for another unforgettable adventure.\r\n\r\nI'd also like to express my sincere gratitude to CD Projekt RED and congratulate the team on the care and respect they've shown toward the community.\r\n\r\nIn an industry where many companies wouldn't think twice about charging full price for a Remastered or Next-Gen edition, you released a massive upgrade packed with improvements completely free of charge for everyone who already owned the original game.\r\n\r\nThis level of appreciation for your fans is becoming increasingly rare, and it deserves to be recognized. Thank you for giving us the perfect reason to return to the Continent and experience this unforgettable journey all over again.\r\n\r\nRating: 10/10 🃏🃏🃏\r\n\r\nCiri is in mortal danger in the middle of a Wild Hunt, but the merchant just asked me if I play Gwent... And well, priorities are priorities, right? Time to bring out my Northern Realms deck!",
